    "legend": "An admixture of two histologically distinct components is seen. One component comprises a diffuse proliferation of small cells with scant pale eosinophilic cytoplasm and relatively uniform hyperchromatic nuclei consistent with blastema, while the second shows moderately differentiated tubules consistent with an epithelial component. There is incipient glomerulus formation (mid upper). No stromal component, necrosis, anaplasia, or heterologous differentiation are observed.",
